# What NOT to upload when deploying with `vercel --prod`.
#
# The CLI uploads the working directory, not the git tree, and without this file that is
# 981 MB: the whole Godot project, its 195 MB addon asset pack, its 107 MB import cache, the
# QA evidence and node_modules. The upload times out and aborts in a loop.
#
# Vercel serves the API, not the game: both GitHub and Vercel refuse any single file over
# 100 MB and index.pck is 189 MB, so the playable build is on itch.io. What Vercel needs is
# api/axie.js (the Axie lookup proxy the browser build calls, because the GraphQL gateway
# sends no CORS headers) and tools/vercel-build.sh. Everything else, web/ included, stays
# off the upload.

godot
production
design
docs
src
assets
third_party
node_modules
.git
.github
.claude
build
web

# Root files that are for the repository, not the deploy.
README.md
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
LICENSE
FINISH.sh
export-web.sh
push-to-github.sh
HANDOFF-PUSH.md
build.py
package.json
package-lock.json
